# Release rehearsal rig parameters — the full parameter surface, no
# secrets committed. Copy to Ctl/rehearsal/rig.env (keep it out of git; it
# will hold token values) and fill in.
#
# rig.env is sourced by stand-up.sh and the later rehearsal scripts. ALL
# rig identity lives here (README.md: "Teardown and re-standup"); nothing
# is hard-coded in the scripts, so ctl adoption is new values + the same
# scripts.
#
# Everything here is rehearsal-only. Never put the production release PAT,
# the production release signing key, or the production repo/project names
# in this file — the offline guard in lib.sh refuses production targets
# (lmer2/lmer, a repo or project named lmer, pypi.org, production release
# credential variables) before any network call.

# Scratch GitHub repo, owner/name, under the bot account that owns the
# production mirror (so repo controls are configured identically).
# Never lmer2/lmer.
LMER_REHEARSAL_REPO="<bot>/lmer-rehearsal"

# TestPyPI project name. Never "lmer" — rehearsal artifacts must be
# unmistakably non-production.
LMER_REHEARSAL_PROJECT="lmer-rehearsal"

# GitHub deployment environment named in the TestPyPI trusted-publisher
# binding. Distinct from production's "pypi" so a rig workflow can never
# satisfy a production binding, and vice versa.
LMER_REHEARSAL_ENVIRONMENT="testpypi"

# Fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to the scratch repo ONLY. The rig needs
# more than the production push scopes because stand-up.sh manages the
# repo itself via the REST API. Repository permissions required:
#   Administration: read+write  (create/delete the scratch repo, rulesets,
#                                environments + deployment branch policies)
#   Contents: read+write        (clone/push main and tags, release lookup)
#   Workflows: read+write       (commit .github/workflows/release.yml)
#   Variables: read+write       (RELEASE_ALLOWED_SIGNERS)
#   Actions: read+write         (poll runs; re-run/cancel in the leg-2
#                                idempotency re-entries)
#   Pull requests: read         (PR-posture report)
# Never the production release PAT.
LMER_REHEARSAL_GITHUB_TOKEN=""

# TestPyPI API token — OPTIONAL, read by no rig script today: stand-up.sh
# verifies the project via TestPyPI's tokenless read-only JSON API, and
# the rig workflow publishes via the trusted publisher (OIDC). Reserved
# for manual TestPyPI maintenance (e.g. deleting rehearsal releases by
# hand); leaving it empty skips nothing.
LMER_REHEARSAL_TESTPYPI_TOKEN=""

# Path to the THROWAWAY ed25519 signing key. stand-up.sh generates it
# here if absent; --teardown discards it. Never the production release
# signing key, and never the production mount path /release-signing-key.
LMER_REHEARSAL_SIGNING_KEY="${HOME}/.ssh/lmer-rehearsal-signing"
